      "writtenOn": "2024-08-13T15:39:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, like cars, tablets also don\u0027t start Bluetooth on their headless user?\n\nSo that would imply you all are the exception and not the rule then, I think. Perhaps some sort of UserManager API or other semantically correct abstraction (`FEATURE_` flag) is the way to go. I think a UserManager API would bring legitimacy to the user pattern you\u0027re trying and is preferred to something like `FEATURE_HSUM_BLUETOOTH`.\n\nThere may be a `FEATURE_*` flag for tablets as well, which can hold you over until something semantically correct is implemented.",
